{%- comment -%}
  PURELANE — PRICE
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The prototype hardcoded every price: ₹200 / ₹299 / "33% off" was literal
  markup repeated on each card, identical across four different products.
  This reads the real price, the real compare-at price, and derives the saving.

  Money is rendered through the `money` filter, so the currency format follows
  the store's own settings rather than a baked-in ₹.

  Handles the states the prototype had no way to express:
    - no compare-at price   → no strikethrough, no saving badge
    - price varies by variant → "From <price>"
    - sold out              → caller decides; see purelane-product-card

  Accepts:
    product   object   required
    variant   object   optional. Prices this variant instead of the product
    saving    string   optional. 'percent' (default) or 'amount'
    class     string   optional. Extra classes on the wrapper

  Usage:
    {% render 'purelane-price', product: card_product %}
    {% render 'purelane-price', product: combo_product, saving: 'amount' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  if variant != blank
    assign price = variant.price
    assign compare_at = variant.compare_at_price
    assign varies = false
  else
    assign price = product.price
    assign compare_at = product.compare_at_price
    assign varies = product.price_varies
  endif

  assign saving_style = saving | default: 'percent'
  assign has_saving = false

  if compare_at > price
    assign has_saving = true
    assign saved_amount = compare_at | minus: price
    assign saved_percent = saved_amount | times: 100.0 | divided_by: compare_at | round
  endif
-%}

<div class="pl-price {{ class }}">
  <strong class="pl-price__now">
    {%- if varies -%}
      {{- 'products.product.from_price_html' | t: price: price | money -}}
      {%- comment -%}
        Dawn ships this translation key; if a theme lacks it the filter falls
        back to the raw price, which still reads correctly.
      {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {{- price | money -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  </strong>

  {%- if has_saving -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The compare-at price is announced to screen readers with its own label,
      because a bare <s> is read as a second, contradictory price.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <s class="pl-price__was">
      <span class="pl-visually-hidden">Regular price </span>
      {{- compare_at | money -}}
    </s>

    <em class="pl-price__save">
      {%- if saving_style == 'amount' -%}
        Save {{ saved_amount | money }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ saved_percent }}% off
      {%- endif -%}
    </em>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
